  "subsequentChanges": "After craft-a3, only paper stripe contrast/signature-cut density and distance LOD changed; final actual-App captures show the small-scale result. Museum/wood geometry and the library architecture stayed unchanged.",
  "observations": [
    "Crafted bronze/wood profiles and book bindings replace basic primitive silhouettes. Thin rounded geometry now has correctly oriented normals.",
    "Wood end surfaces use planar UVs without radial pinching; material grain is finer and reflection/roughness variation is restrained.",
    "Library has three real depth layers, detailed books, gallery, window recesses, parquet/coffers and owned contact cues. Camera and canonical globe remain unchanged.",
    "Phone-scale signature-cut moire is removed with near-only detail and filtered paper surface maps. The renderer automatically selects that LOD with hysteresis.",
    "Same actual canvas/renderer/camera, locale and semantic selection survive preview/cancel/apply and real WebGL recovery. Observed retired textures/geometry/materials/instances are disposed once.",
    "Appearance controls, including truthful save retry, fit tested390/320 widths with at least44px controls."
  ],
